## Context
PR #88 moved `loadBranchNames()` (one `git branch -a` spawn) before the
ticket loop — unconditional even when all tickets are blocked or tagged.
On some machines `git branch -a` takes ~2s (credential helper, SSH timeout,
fsmonitor daemon).  This produces a fixed ~2s regression independent of
ticket count, reported against .claude (87 tickets, +1.95s) and aedist
(28 tickets, +1.84s).

The old per-ticket code only spawned git when a ticket was open AND unblocked.
Repos where everything is tagged/blocked got 0 git spawns.  The new code
always spawns once.

## Actions
1. Replace `branches := loadBranchNames()` (unconditional) with lazy
   initialization inside the loop — only load on first unblocked ticket:
   ```go
   var branches []string
   branchesLoaded := false
   ...
   if !blocked {
       if !branchesLoaded {
           branches = loadBranchNames()
           branchesLoaded = true
       }
       claimed = isBranchClaimed(tid, branches)
   }
   ```

## Test
- `make test-ready` green
- Repo where all tickets are blocked: `strace` shows 0 git spawns
- Repo with at least one unblocked ticket: `strace` shows exactly 1 git spawn

## Exit criteria
- 0 git spawns when every ticket is blocked/tagged
- 1 git spawn (max) when any ticket is unblocked
- All 21 ready tests pass
